# Build directories
# Convention: build-{linux,windows,macos} are the per-OS canonical dirs
# created by scripts/setup.sh. Legacy names are kept ignored for old checkouts.
build/
build-*/
builddir/
builddir-*/
clion-build/
cmake-build-*/
out/
.cache/

# Agent-bundle delivery image: build context staged by scripts/build-agent-bundle.sh
# (downloaded release archives + the laid-out /opt/yuzu-agents tree). Large, derived.
deploy/docker/.agent-bundle-build/

# Erlang / rebar3
# `_build/` is the canonical rebar3 base dir. `_build_eunit/` and
# `_build_ct/` are per-suite base dirs set via REBAR_BASE_DIR in
# meson.build so parallel meson test invocations don't race on a
# shared ebin tree (Windows `.bea#`→`.beam` rename race in `proper`).
gateway/_build/
gateway/_build_eunit/
gateway/_build_eunit_test/
gateway/_build_ct/
gateway/_build_ct_realup/
gateway/.deps_cache/
gateway/ebin/
erl_crash.dump
*.beam

# Meson
.mesonpy/
meson-info/
meson-logs/
meson-private/
compile_commands.json

# vcpkg — match the dir AND the worktree cache-share symlink (a bare
# `vcpkg_installed/` trailing slash matches directories only, so a symlink
# slipped past `git add -A` and got tracked; `/vcpkg_installed` matches both).
/vcpkg_installed

# Binaries
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.a
*.lib
*.pdb
*.obj

# Generated protobuf sources
*.pb.h
*.pb.cc
*.grpc.pb.h
*.grpc.pb.cc

# IDE / Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.clangd/
CLion.ini

# Secrets / credentials (defence-in-depth alongside GitHub Advanced Secret
# Scanning push-protection — stops accidental staging before it reaches a
# remote). No such files are currently tracked; if you ever need to commit
# a fixture with one of these extensions (e.g. an intentional test PEM),
# add a path-specific negation below this block.
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# UAT runtime state
.uat/
bash.exe.stackdump

# Dev artifacts
_build_tmp.bat
_debug_vcvars.bat
_vcvars_env.txt
build_now.bat
build_now.ps1
meson_stderr.txt
meson_stdout.txt
_build_err.txt
_build_out.txt
build_log.txt
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.mcp.json
.uat-sanitizer/
*.local.md
*.local.MD
# hookify rule files (.claude/hookify.*.local.md) are intentionally shared with
# the team despite the *.local.md suffix — negate the ignore so they're tracked.
!.claude/hookify.*.local.md
docker-compose.local.yml
.codex/*
!.codex/skills/
!.codex/skills/**
test_output.txt
test_xml.txt
update.finished
node_modules/
__pycache__/

# Test-binary symlinks created by scripts/link-tests.sh
# (per-component, per-triplet convenience links — see CLAUDE.md Test section)
/tests-build-*/

# /test pipeline scratch state (per-run RUN_ID directories)
# Persistent test-runs DB lives outside the repo at
# ~/.local/share/yuzu/test-runs.db — see .claude/skills/test/SKILL.md
/tests/.last-test-run/

# Future PR2 artifacts (coverage + sanitizer build dirs)
/build-linux-coverage/
/build-linux-asan/
/build-linux-tsan/

# Per-host runner verification script. Stays local on each runner
# host because the operator-visible defaults (WSL distro, WSL user,
# tmux session name, expected NordVPN/Meshnet posture, expected
# Defender exclusion set) are tuned to that specific host's
# operator account and aren't generally useful across deployments.
# Sibling scripts that ARE generic (windows-runner-defender-
# exclusions.ps1 with its host-allowlist guard, the autologon-
# diagnose script) stay tracked.
/scripts/windows-runner-status.ps1

# One-off scratch tool — ASCII histograms over perf-sample JSONL output.
# Useful for eyeballing distribution shape (skew, outliers, multimodality)
# but not part of the gated pipeline; perf-stats.py is the canonical
# stats consumer of perf-baseline-provenance-*.jsonl.
/scripts/test/perf-histograms.py

.screenshots/

# Local Darwin-native shims for Linux/WSL-only helpers in scripts/.
# These exist only on macOS dev boxes and replace upstream scripts that
# refuse to run under zsh or assume Linux toolchain layout (e.g. kerl
# activation, ss/df flags, /var/lib/docker). Per the Darwin policy in
# CLAUDE.md the shims are local-only — never tracked.
/scripts/darwin-*.sh

# Per-repo configuration for the Matt Pocock engineering skills
# (issue-tracker mapping, triage-label vocabulary, domain-doc index).
# Generated by /setup-matt-pocock-skills; references local labels and
# tooling preferences that shouldn't bind teammates.
/docs/agents/
!/docs/agents/
!/docs/agents/*.md
.aider*
.lora/

# Server runtime artifacts written to the working dir on launch.
# enrollment-tokens.cfg holds live enrollment tokens (secrets); pending-agents.cfg
# is transient enrollment state. Never track either.
enrollment-tokens.cfg
pending-agents.cfg

# Commercially sensitive planning docs — local-only, never commit
docs/dex-brd-coverage.md

# Local-only working directories — scratch notes, throwaway spikes, agent
# skill-install stray targets, and personal tuning prefs. Never track.
.scratch/
.lora-prefs/
.agents/
spike/

# Local runtime SQLite databases (large, reconstructable — never commit; a dev
# --data-dir pointed in-tree must not commit the catalog). PR2b.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# ...but never silently hide an intentionally-committed test fixture DB (#1889
# review): the broad *.db net above would otherwise drop it from `git add`.
!tests/**/*.db

# promtool canary scratch tree (created and removed by
# tests/prometheus/run_promtool_tests.py; a fresh mkdtemp per gate() call
# since #2340 PR-4, so only a killed run leaves one of these behind)
.promtool-canary-*/

# marker-extracted yuzu-guardian-journal rules (#2340 PR-4), materialized
# fresh on every run by tests/prometheus/run_promtool_tests.py from the
# commented block in docs/prometheus/yuzu-alerts.yml - never committed
tests/prometheus/generated/
